data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:42:04.073052+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_6e3dfd285d2f462f", "event_type": "react.step.completed", "session_id": "sess_be7e4295c87a", "workspace_id": "ws_9f03590dd4d4", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_0d94515cedad", "turn_id": "msg_user_0d94515cedad", "span_id": "sem_6e3dfd285d2f462f", "parent_span_id": "69ae7038e56148c1", "status": "completed", "summary": "geospatial ReAct step 1: finish", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:42:04.072386+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "geospatial", "role": "expert"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {}, "provider": {}, "payload": {"expert_id": "geospatial", "expert_span_id": "69ae7038e56148c1", "step_span_id": "72369ccc3e6e404f", "step_index": 1, "thought": "The geo_geocode tool successfully resolved \"Los Angeles, California\" to a grounded location. I have:\n- Center: lat=34.0536909, lon=-118.242766\n- Bounding box: [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306] (format: [min_lon, min_lat, max_lon, max_lat])\n- Provenance: osm_nominatim (authentic OpenStreetMap lookup)\n- Confidence: high (administrative boundary, importance=0.84)\n\nThe request did not specify a search radius, so I must choose a conservative regional-analysis radius. For seismic events and GNSS station discovery around LA, a 100 km radius is standard practice\u2014it covers the Los Angeles Basin, surrounding seismic networks (San Gabriel, San Bernardino, etc.), and satellite stations in the greater Southern California region. This is appropriate for both recent earthquake context and GNSS deformation analysis. I'll record this as an assumed default in warnings.\n\nI have all the geospatial evidence needed. Now I finish and return the structured workflow_state.", "reasoning": "", "tool_name": "finish", "tool_args": {}, "observation": "Completed.", "is_finish": true}}}

