data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:42:21.534298+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_f04ec3f4580e4771", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_be7e4295c87a", "workspace_id": "ws_9f03590dd4d4", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_0d94515cedad", "turn_id": "msg_user_0d94515cedad", "span_id": "sem_f04ec3f4580e4771", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert geospatial produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:42:21.532747+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "geospatial"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "main"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "geospatial", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'geospatial'.", "answer": "Geographic region resolved from place name \"Los Angeles\" via OpenStreetMap Nominatim geocoding.\n\n**Center:** 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W (Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States)\n\n**Search radius:** 100 km (assumed default for regional GNSS and seismic analysis; not specified in request)\n\n**Bounding box:** [\u2212118.6681798, 33.659541, \u2212118.1552983, 34.337306] (min_lon, min_lat, max_lon, max_lat)\n\n**Confidence:** high (administrative boundary, OSM importance 0.84)\n\n**Provenance:** osm_nominatim (OpenStreetMap Nominatim lookup, grounded coordinates)\n\n**Warnings:** Search radius of 100 km assumed as default for regional GNSS and seismic analysis; not specified in request.", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [{"name": "geo_geocode", "args": {"query": "Los Angeles, California", "limit": 1, "countrycodes": "us"}, "ok": true, "telemetry_source": "agent_trajectory", "result": "[{'display_name': 'Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States', 'lat': 34.0536909, 'lon': -118.242766, 'bbox': [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], 'type': 'administrative', 'importance': 0.8410828881088647, 'provenance': 'osm_nominatim'}]"}, {"name": "finish", "args": {}, "ok": true, "telemetry_source": "agent_trajectory", "result": "Completed."}, {"name": "clio_prior_workflow_state", "args": {}, "ok": true, "telemetry_source": "blueprint_react_context_seed"}, {"name": "geo_geocode", "args": {"query": "Los Angeles, California", "limit": 1, "countrycodes": "us"}, "ok": true, "duration_ms": 747.1001689846162, "telemetry_source": "blueprint_react_tool_wrapper", "result": "[{'display_name': 'Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States', 'lat': 34.0536909, 'lon': -118.242766, 'bbox': [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], 'type': 'administrative', 'importance': 0.8410828881088647, 'provenance': 'osm_nominatim'}]"}], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "trajectory": {"thought_0": "The request asks me to resolve \"Los Angeles\" into a geographic region. I have a place name, not explicit coordinates, so I need to call `geo_geocode` to look up the real coordinates and bounding box from OpenStreetMap Nominatim. This will give me a grounded center (lat/lon) and regional extent. After the tool returns, I'll extract the center, choose a search radius appropriate for GNSS station and seismic event discovery in the LA region, and finish with the structured geospatial evidence.", "tool_name_0": "geo_geocode", "tool_args_0": {"query": "Los Angeles, California", "limit": 1, "countrycodes": "us"}, "observation_0": "[{'display_name': 'Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States', 'lat': 34.0536909, 'lon': -118.242766, 'bbox': [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], 'type': 'administrative', 'importance': 0.8410828881088647, 'provenance': 'osm_nominatim'}]", "thought_1": "The geo_geocode tool successfully resolved \"Los Angeles, California\" to a grounded location. I have:\n- Center: lat=34.0536909, lon=-118.242766\n- Bounding box: [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306] (format: [min_lon, min_lat, max_lon, max_lat])\n- Provenance: osm_nominatim (authentic OpenStreetMap lookup)\n- Confidence: high (administrative boundary, importance=0.84)\n\nThe request did not specify a search radius, so I must choose a conservative regional-analysis radius. For seismic events and GNSS station discovery around LA, a 100 km radius is standard practice\u2014it covers the Los Angeles Basin, surrounding seismic networks (San Gabriel, San Bernardino, etc.), and satellite stations in the greater Southern California region. This is appropriate for both recent earthquake context and GNSS deformation analysis. I'll record this as an assumed default in warnings.\n\nI have all the geospatial evidence needed. Now I finish and return the structured workflow_state.", "tool_name_1": "finish", "tool_args_1": {}, "observation_1": "Completed."}, "reasoning": "The geospatial expert successfully resolved the place name \"Los Angeles\" by calling the `geo_geocode` tool with the query \"Los Angeles, California\" and country code \"us\". The tool returned a grounded OpenStreetMap Nominatim match: Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States at coordinates 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W. This is an administrative boundary with high importance (0.84), giving high confidence in the center location.\n\nThe request did not specify a search radius, so following the system instructions, a conservative regional-analysis radius of 100 km was chosen as the default. This radius appropriately covers the Los Angeles Basin, surrounding seismic networks (San Gabriel, San Bernardino), and the broader Southern California GNSS station network, suitable for both recent seismic event discovery and GNSS deformation analysis. The bounding box from the OSM lookup is retained as reference context. The assumed radius default is recorded in warnings per protocol."}}}

