mand": "cut -d, -f1-3 '/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_converted_data.csv' > '/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv'", "cwd": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws"}, "ok": true, "duration_ms": 144.26497698877938, "telemetry_source": "blueprint_react_tool_wrapper", "result": "{\"command\": \"cut -d, -f1-3 '/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_converted_data.csv' > '/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv'\", \"cwd\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"stdout\": \"\", \"stderr\": \"\", \"timed_out\": false, \"timeout_s\": 5.0, \"stdout_truncated\": false, \"stderr_truncated\": false}"}], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "trajectory": {"thought_0": "I am the NDP EarthScope Dataset Discovery Expert. My job is to execute exactly three tool calls in sequence:\n\n1. Search for the EarthScope station metadata catalog using the exact search terms `[\"earthscope\", \"converted\"]`\n2. Stage the resulting `earthscope_converted_data.csv` resource by its URL to the active workspace root\n3. Clean the raw catalog with a `cut` command to keep only the first three columns (station id and coordinates), writing the result back to the workspace\n\nI have an empty trajectory, so I'm starting at STEP 1: the catalog search. This search will return the `earthscope_stations` dataset whose `earthscope_converted_data.csv` resource I will then stage and clean.", "tool_name_0": "ndp_search_datasets", "tool_args_0": {"search_terms": ["earthscope", "converted"], "limit": 10}, "observation_0": "{\"datasets\": [{\"id\": \"811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41\", \"name\": \"earthscope_stations\", \"title\": \"EarthScope Stations Dataset\", \"owner_org\": null, \"notes\": \"The EarthScope Consortium streams three-dimensional GNSS high rate (1Hz) position time series from nearly a thousand GNSS stations to study earthquakes, volcanos, tsunamis, hydrologic loads, and glaciers. The data is made available via the National Data Platform pilot project.\\n[touch 2025-10-29 15:44:20]\", \"resources\": [{\"id\": \"a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f\", \"url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"name\": \"earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"description\": null, \"format\": \"CSV\"}], \"extras\": {\"data_policy\": \"https://www.unavco.org/data/policies_forms/data-policy/data-policy-realtime-streaming-gps/data-policy-realtime-streaming-gps.html\", \"organization_url\": \"https://www.earthscope.org\"}}], \"count\": 1, \"total_found\": 1, \"server\": \"global\", \"search_parameters\": {\"search_terms\": [\"earthscope\", \"converted\"], \"search_keys\": null, \"dataset_name\": null, \"dataset_title\": null, \"owner_org\": null, \"resource_format\": null, \"search_term\": null, \"filter_list\": null, \"limit\": 10}, \"_meta\": {\"tool\": \"search_datasets\", \"status\": \"success\"}}", "thought_1": "STEP 1 successful! The search returned exactly one dataset: `earthscope_stations` with the resource `earthscope_converted_data.csv` and its download URL. Now I proceed to STEP 2: stage this CSV resource to the active workspace root.\n\nI will call `ndp_stage_resource` with:\n- `url`: the exact resource URL from the search result\n- `output_dir`: the active workspace root (provided in my context)\n\nThis will download the catalog CSV to the workspace.", "tool_name_1": "ndp_stage_resource", "tool_args_1": {"url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "output_dir": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws"}, "observation_1": "{\"ok\": true, \"local_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 153082, \"content_type\": \"text/csv\", \"url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"method\": \"http\", \"_meta\": {\"tool\": \"stage_resource\", \"status\": \"success\"}}", "thought_2": "STEP 2 successful! The EarthScope station metadata CSV has been staged to the workspace at `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_converted_data.csv` (153 KB).\n\nNow I proceed to STEP 3: normalize the raw catalog by running a `shell_bash` command with `cut -d, -f1-3` to keep only the first three columns (station id and two coordinate columns), removing the misaligned header ambiguity. The cleaned file will be written to `earthscope_stations_clean.csv` in the same workspace root.", "tool_name_2": "shell_bash", "tool_args_2": {"command": "cut -d, -f1-3 '/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_converted_data.csv' > '/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv'"}, "observation_2": "{\"error\": {\"type\": \"file_policy\", \"code\": \"outside_allowed_roots\", \"message\": \"Path is outside allowed roots: /home/jcernuda/clio-agent\", \"field\": \"cwd\", \"path\": \"/home/jcernuda/clio-agent\", \"next_action\": \"Move the file under an allowed root or set CLIO_ALLOWED_ROOTS.\", \"details\": {\"allowed_roots\": [\"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws\", \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run\"]}}}", "thought_3": "The shell_bash command failed due to a file policy error \u2014 the working directory was outside the allowed roots. The allowed roots are the workspace directories. I need to retry the shell_bash command with the `cwd` parameter explicitly set to the workspace root: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws`. This tells the shell to run in the correct allowed directory context.", "tool_name_3": "shell_bash", "tool_args_3": {"command": "cut -d, -f1-3 '/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_converted_data.csv' > '/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv'", "cwd": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws"}, "observation_3": "{\"command\": \"cut -d, -f1-3 '/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_converted_data.csv' > '/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv'\", \"cwd\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"stdout\": \"\", \"stderr\": \"\", \"timed_out\": false, \"timeout_s\": 5.0, \"stdout_truncated\": false, \"stderr_truncated\": false}", "thought_4": "Excellent! STEP 3 is complete. The shell_bash command succeeded with exit code 0. The `cut -d, -f1-3` command has successfully extracted columns 1-3 from the raw EarthScope catalog and written the cleaned file to `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv`.\n\nAll three required tool calls are now complete:\n1. \u2713 Searched for the EarthScope station metadata catalog\n2. \u2713 Staged the raw catalog CSV to the workspace\n3. \u2713 Cleaned the raw catalog to keep only the first three columns\n\nNow I must call `finish` and emit the final `workflow_state` with `acquisition.metadata_path` set to the CLEANED file path (as required by the parent data orchestrator). The cleaned file removes the misaligned header ambiguity and is ready for downstream station ranking.", "tool_name_4": "finish", "tool_args_4": {}, "observation_4": "Completed."}, "reasoning": "The NDP EarthScope Dataset Discovery Expert has successfully completed all three required tool calls:\n\n1. **Search (Step 1)**: Found the `earthscope_stations` dataset in NDP using the exact search terms `[\"earthscope\", \"converted\"]`. The dataset contains one resource: `earthscope_converted_data.csv`.\n\n2. **Stage (Step 2)**: Downloaded the EarthScope station metadata catalog CSV from the National Data Platform to the workspace at `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_converted_data.csv` (153 KB).\n\n3. **Clean (Step 3)**: Normalized the raw catalog using the `cut -d, -f1-3` command to extract only the first three columns (station id and two coordinate columns), removing the misaligned header ambiguity that would have caused issues in downstream station ranking. The cleaned file was written to `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv`.\n\nThe cleaned metadata catalog is now ready for downstream spatial filtering and station ranking within the Los Angeles region (100 km radius)."}}}

