data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:44:12.170343+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_823caa9b45424209", "event_type": "react.step.completed", "session_id": "sess_be7e4295c87a", "workspace_id": "ws_9f03590dd4d4", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_0d94515cedad", "turn_id": "msg_user_0d94515cedad", "span_id": "sem_823caa9b45424209", "parent_span_id": "24b3500b4cfa4f48", "status": "completed", "summary": "earthscope_station_catalog ReAct step 1: geo_filter_points_by_radius", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:44:12.166073+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "earthscope_station_catalog", "role": "expert"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {}, "provider": {}, "payload": {"expert_id": "earthscope_station_catalog", "expert_span_id": "24b3500b4cfa4f48", "step_span_id": "ddb6cf7a18e34204", "step_index": 1, "thought": "Perfect! I can see the cleaned catalog structure:\n- Column 1: `Site` (station IDs: 7ODM, ACSB, ACSV, AGMT, etc.)\n- Column 2: `Latitude` (latitude values: 34.11640827, 33.27426630, etc. \u2014 in range [-90,90])\n- Column 3: `(deg)` (longitude values: -117.09319697, -117.44489491, etc. \u2014 in range [-180,180])\n\nThe header `(deg)` for longitude is exactly the misaligned header the instructions warned about. I've verified the column VALUES, not just headers:\n- Column 2 contains latitudes (34\u00b0-33\u00b0 range, close to LA center 34.05\u00b0)\n- Column 3 contains longitudes (-117\u00b0 to -116\u00b0 range, close to LA center -118.24\u00b0)\n\nNow I'll call `geo_filter_points_by_radius` with explicit column names:\n- `id_column` = \"Site\"\n- `lat_column` = \"Latitude\"\n- `lon_column` = \"(deg)\"\n- Center: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W\n- Radius: 100 km (use the exact resolved radius, never widen)", "reasoning": "", "tool_name": "geo_filter_points_by_radius", "tool_args": {"data_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6