event: message.part.delta
id: 106
data: {"type": "message.part.delta", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:44:54.995614+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_0d94515cedad", "message_id": "msg_asst_ccd8c7ddaab2", "part_id": "part_df074a4d40e1", "stream_source": "live", "delta": {"text_append": "Ranked EarthScope GNSS Station Candidates for Los Angeles (100 km radius):\n\n**Coverage Summary**: 155 nearby stations identified within 100 km of Los Angeles center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W).\n\n**Top 10 Closest Stations** (suitable for detailed analysis):\n1. MTA1 - 0.3 km (downtown LA area)\n2. PKRD - 2.2 km (close to center)\n3. ELSC - 4.1 km \n4. USC2 - 5.0 km (USC campus area)\n5. SILK - 5.8 km\n6. OXYC - 9.0 km\n7. P800 - 10.4 km\n8. LEE2 - 11.6 km\n9. LEEP - 11.6 km\n10. GVRS - 11.9 km\n\n**Extended Coverage**: 145 additional stations provide excellent spatial redundancy extending to 99.7 km radius, covering the greater Los Angeles basin, surrounding mountains, and coastal regions. This density of observations is ideal for resolving seismic deformation patterns from recent earthquakes and ongoing strain accumulation.\n\n**Next Step**: The resource resolver will search NDP for concrete station time-series CSV resources for these ranked candidates, starting with the closest stations for priority processing.\n\n"}}}

