itude values: 34.11640827, 33.27426630, etc. \u2014 in range [-90,90])\n- Column 3: `(deg)` (longitude values: -117.09319697, -117.44489491, etc. \u2014 in range [-180,180])\n\nThe header `(deg)` for longitude is exactly the misaligned header the instructions warned about. I've verified the column VALUES, not just headers:\n- Column 2 contains latitudes (34\u00b0-33\u00b0 range, close to LA center 34.05\u00b0)\n- Column 3 contains longitudes (-117\u00b0 to -116\u00b0 range, close to LA center -118.24\u00b0)\n\nNow I'll call `geo_filter_points_by_radius` with explicit column names:\n- `id_column` = \"Site\"\n- `lat_column` = \"Latitude\"\n- `lon_column` = \"(deg)\"\n- Center: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W\n- Radius: 100 km (use the exact resolved radius, never widen)", "tool_name_1": "geo_filter_points_by_radius", "tool_args_1": {"data_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "radius_km": 100, "lat_column": "Latitude", "lon_column": "(deg)", "id_column": "Site", "compact": true}, "observation_1": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 155, \"within_radius_count\": 155, \"total_points\": 1101, \"skipped_invalid\": 0, \"source_format\": \"csv\", \"lat_column\": \"Latitude\", \"lon_column\": \"(deg)\", \"center\": {\"lat\": 34.0536909, \"lon\": -118.242766}, \"radius_km\": 100.0, \"points\": [{\"distance_km\": 0.3045, \"id\": \"MTA1\", \"Site\": \"MTA1\"}, {\"distance_km\": 2.1848, \"id\": \"PKRD\", \"Site\": \"PKRD\"}, {\"distance_km\": 4.1351, \"id\": \"ELSC\", \"Site\": \"ELSC\"}, {\"distance_km\": 4.9583, \"id\": \"USC2\", \"Site\": \"USC2\"}, {\"distance_km\": 5.8032, \"id\": \"SILK\", \"Site\": \"SILK\"}, {\"distance_km\": 8.9684, \"id\": \"OXYC\", \"Site\": \"OXYC\"}, {\"distance_km\": 10.4218, \"id\": \"P800\", \"Site\": \"P800\"}, {\"distance_km\": 11.5697, \"id\": \"LEE2\", \"Site\": \"LEE2\"}, {\"distance_km\": 11.5697, \"i