471\"}, {\"distance_km\": 85.791, \"id\": \"LMHG\", \"Site\": \"LMHG\"}, {\"distance_km\": 86.5833, \"id\": \"MLFP\", \"Site\": \"MLFP\"}, {\"distance_km\": 86.641, \"id\": \"P612\", \"Site\": \"P612\"}, {\"distance_km\": 87.8182, \"id\": \"ELSG\", \"Site\": \"ELSG\"}, {\"distance_km\": 88.1255, \"id\": \"OVLS\", \"Site\": \"OVLS\"}, {\"distance_km\": 88.4353, \"id\": \"HIVI\", \"Site\": \"HIVI\"}, {\"distance_km\": 89.0394, \"id\": \"ECFS\", \"Site\": \"ECFS\"}, {\"distance_km\": 89.4471, \"id\": \"P577\", \"Site\": \"P577\"}, {\"distance_km\": 89.582, \"id\": \"RMVJ\", \"Site\": \"RMVJ\"}, {\"distance_km\": 89.6796, \"id\": \"P560\", \"Site\": \"P560\"}, {\"distance_km\": 90.2864, \"id\": \"P470\", \"Site\": \"P470\"}, {\"distance_km\": 90.6974, \"id\": \"P582\", \"Site\": \"P582\"}, {\"distance_km\": 90.9706, \"id\": \"RCSC\", \"Site\": \"RCSC\"}, {\"distance_km\": 91.4488, \"id\": \"RSTP\", \"Site\": \"RSTP\"}, {\"distance_km\": 91.7639, \"id\": \"TPOG\", \"Site\": \"TPOG\"}, {\"distance_km\": 93.6659, \"id\": \"P808\", \"Site\": \"P808\"}, {\"distance_km\": 94.8093, \"id\": \"VNCO\", \"Site\": \"VNCO\"}, {\"distance_km\": 95.2076, \"id\": \"ALPP\", \"Site\": \"ALPP\"}, {\"distance_km\": 96.2485, \"id\": \"NHRG\", \"Site\": \"NHRG\"}, {\"distance_km\": 96.7199, \"id\": \"BAR1\", \"Site\": \"BAR1\"}, {\"distance_km\": 96.9436, \"id\": \"HVYS\", \"Site\": \"HVYS\"}, {\"distance_km\": 97.0534, \"id\": \"MSOB\", \"Site\": \"MSOB\"}, {\"distance_km\": 97.8969, \"id\": \"SONG\", \"Site\": \"SONG\"}, {\"distance_km\": 99.1327, \"id\": \"P554\", \"Site\": \"P554\"}, {\"distance_km\": 99.7366, \"id\": \"SCIA\", \"Site\": \"SCIA\"}]}", "thought_2": "Excellent! The geo_filter_points_by_radius tool succeeded with outstanding results:\n- **within_radius_count**: 155 stations within the 100 km radius\n- **skipped_invalid**: 0 (all rows parsed correctly)\n- **points**: 155 within-radius stations, sorted by distance ascending\n\nThis is exceptional EarthScope GNSS coverage for the Los Angeles region! The closest stations are:\n1. MTA1 (0.3 km) - almost at the center!\n2. PKRD (2.2 km)\n3. ELSC (4.1 km)\n4. USC2 (5.0 km)\n5. SILK (5.8 km)\n\nAnd 150 more stations extending up to 99.7 km away.\n\nAccording to the instructions, I should emit:\n- `station_catalog.status=ranked` (since within_radius_count >= 1)\n- `station_catalog.station_ids` as a flat list of all 155 station IDs\n- `resource_discovery.station_resource_queries` with preferred NDP search calls for top candidates\n- The parent `data` orchestrator will advance to `ndp_resource_resolver` to stage the selected stations\n\nNow I'll construct the final workflow_state and call finish.", "tool_name_2": "finish", "tool_args_2": {}, "observation_2": "Completed."}, "reasoning": "The geo_filter_points_by_radius tool successfully filtered the cleaned EarthScope station metadata catalog using the verified column names (Site, Latitude, (deg)) and the Los Angeles region center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W) with the resolved 100 km radius. Results show exceptional GNSS coverage in the region:\n\n- **within_radius_count**: 155 stations (out of 1101 total)\n- **skipped_invalid**: 0 (perfect parsing with explicit column names)\n- **Closest stations**: MTA1 (0.3 km), PKRD (2.2 km), ELSC (4.1 km), USC2 (5.0 km), SILK (5.8 km)\n- **Coverage extends** to 99.7 km (SCIA), providing excellent spatial density for seismic deformation analysis\n\nThis is outstanding EarthScope GNSS coverage for the Los Angeles metropolitan region, with stations ranging from downtown LA to the surrounding San Gabriel Mountains, Orange County, and beyond. The dense station network spans multiple networks and provides excellent redundancy for seismic event analysis."}}}

