data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:45:21.013327+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_57924971f15e4886", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_be7e4295c87a", "workspace_id": "ws_9f03590dd4d4", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_0d94515cedad", "turn_id": "msg_user_0d94515cedad", "span_id": "sem_57924971f15e4886", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert data produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:45:21.007631+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "data"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "main"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "data", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'data'.", "answer": "(To be populated after ndp_resource_resolver stages the station time-series CSV.)", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "The data orchestrator has received completed results from two child experts:\n\n1. **ndp_dataset_discovery** (\u2713 complete): Successfully staged the cleaned EarthScope station metadata catalog at the workspace, providing the foundation for station ranking.\n\n2. **earthscope_station_catalog** (\u2713 complete): Successfully ranked 155 nearby GNSS stations within the 100 km radius of Los Angeles. The ranking spans from MTA1 at 0.3 km (nearly at the city center) to SCIA at 99.7 km (edge of region), providing excellent spatial coverage for seismic deformation analysis.\n\n**Current state:**\n- Geospatial region: resolved (Los Angeles, 100 km radius)\n- Metadata catalog: staged and ranked\n- Station ranking: 155 candidates identified in order of proximity\n- Data acquisition: **NOT YET STAGED** \u2014 `acquisition.status` is still \"metadata_only\"\n\n**Decision:** According to the data acquisition rules, the workflow is **not complete** when stations are ranked. I must continue to the next required child expert: `ndp_resource_resolver`, which will search NDP for and stage the actual station time-series CSV data (with time, east, north, up columns) suitable for analysis.\n\nThe resolver should prioritize the closest, most accessible stations (MTA1, PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK) to maximize data availability for the seismic deformation analysis."}}}

