event: message.part.delta
id: 199
data: {"type": "message.part.delta", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:48:51.203364+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_0d94515cedad", "message_id": "msg_asst_ccd8c7ddaab2", "part_id": "part_e36b0d0a3b20", "stream_source": "live", "delta": {"text_append": "**MTA1 Station Suitability Assessment for Los Angeles Seismic Deformation Analysis**\n\n**Station Selection Rationale:**\nMTA1 is geographically optimal for capturing Los Angeles-area seismic deformation, positioned at the city center (0.3 km from region center, 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W) within a dense 155-station EarthScope network spanning 100 km radius.\n\n**Resource Evidence:**\n- Staged CSV: MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv (50.4 MB, 250,000 rows)\n- Network: CI (California Integrated Seismic Network)\n- Required columns: all present \u2713\n- Data rows: 250,000 available for analysis\n\n**Measurement Characteristics (Profiled Sample):**\n- Horizontal displacement uncertainties: 3.2\u20133.6 cm (east/north components)\n- Vertical displacement uncertainty: 6.2\u20136.6 cm\n- Displacement ranges: east (\u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m), north (0.029\u20130.058 m), up (0.051\u20130.224 m)\n- Null values in profiled rows: zero across all columns\n- Sample temporal spacing: ~1-second local cadence (unverified for full file)\n\n**Network Context & Redundancy:**\n- Closest station by far within the ranked 155-candidate network\n- Alternative stations for cross-validation within 6 km: PKRD (2.2 km), ELSC (4.1 km), USC2 (5.0 km)\n- Excellent network density supports multi-station deformation analysis if required\n\n**Limitations & Caveats:**\n- Profile scope: scan-limited to 5,000 rows (profiled of 250,000 total)\n- Full-file cadence, duration, gap analysis, and data completeness NOT verified\n- Vertical uncertainties (~6.5 cm) are centimeter-scale, appropriate but not sub-centimeter\n- qChannel quality flag is opaque without decoding\n- Metadata timestamp range (2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12) from resource metadata, not tool-verified\n\n**Suitability Conclusion:**\nMTA1 provides geographically grounded, centimeter-precision displacement measurements suitable for preliminary seismic deformation analysis in Los Angeles. Full-file temporal continuity and processing latency remain unverified. The station is recommended as the primary analysis platform for this workflow.\n\n"}}}

