id: 200
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:48:51.251103+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_6863a0e3ca954fd7", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_be7e4295c87a", "workspace_id": "ws_9f03590dd4d4", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_0d94515cedad", "turn_id": "msg_user_0d94515cedad", "span_id": "sem_6863a0e3ca954fd7", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert station_network_analysis produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:48:51.232483+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "station_network_analysis"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "analysis"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "station_network_analysis", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'station_network_analysis'.", "answer": "**MTA1 Station Suitability Assessment for Los Angeles Seismic Deformation Analysis**\n\n**Station Selection Rationale:**\nMTA1 is geographically optimal for capturing Los Angeles-area seismic deformation, positioned at the city center (0.3 km from region center, 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W) within a dense 155-station EarthScope network spanning 100 km radius.\n\n**Resource Evidence:**\n- Staged CSV: MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv (50.4 MB, 250,000 rows)\n- Network: CI (California Integrated Seismic Network)\n- Required columns: all present \u2713\n- Data rows: 250,000 available for analysis\n\n**Measurement Characteristics (Profiled Sample):**\n- Horizontal displacement uncertainties: 3.2\u20133.6 cm (east/north components)\n- Vertical displacement uncertainty: 6.2\u20136.6 cm\n- Displacement ranges: east (\u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m), north (0.029\u20130.058 m), up (0.051\u20130.224 m)\n- Null values in profiled rows: zero across all columns\n- Sample temporal spacing: ~1-second local cadence (unverified for full file)\n\n**Network Context & Redundancy:**\n- Closest station by far within the ranked 155-candidate network\n- Alternative stations for cross-validation within 6 km: PKRD (2.2 km), ELSC (4.1 km), USC2 (5.0 km)\n- Excellent network density supports multi-station deformation analysis if required\n\n**Limitations & Caveats:**\n- Profile scope: scan-limited to 5,000 rows (profiled of 250,000 total)\n- Full-file cadence, duration, gap analysis, and data completeness NOT verified\n- Vertical uncertainties (~6.5 cm) are centimeter-scale, appropriate but not sub-centimeter\n- qChannel quality flag is opaque without decoding\n- Metadata timestamp range (2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12) from resource metadata, not tool-verified\n\n**Suitability Conclusion:**\nMTA1 provides geographically grounded, centimeter-precision displacement measurements suitable for preliminary seismic deformation analysis in Los Angeles. Full-file temporal continuity and processing latency remain unverified. The station is recommended as the primary analysis platform for this workflow.", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "The station_network_analysis expert evaluates MTA1's suitability using available typed evidence:\n\n**Geographic Context:**\n- MTA1 is the closest ranked station at 0.3 km from Los Angeles center (34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W)\n- Located in downtown LA, geographically grounded in the city core\n- Part of a dense 155-station network within 100 km radius, providing excellent regional coverage\n- Alternative nearby candidates for cross-check: PKRD (2.2 km), ELSC (4.1 km), USC2 (5.0 km)\n\n**Data Completeness & Resource Availability:**\n- Staged CSV: MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv contains 250,000 rows (substantial dataset)\n- All required GNSS displacement columns present (time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel)\n- Zero null values detected in the 5,000-row profiled sample\n- File size (50.4 MB) supports processing for regional analysis\n\n**Measurement Quality (Profiled Evidence):**\n- Horizontal displacement uncertainties: 3.2\u20133.6 cm (centimeter-scale, profiled rows)\n- Vertical displacement uncertainties: 6.2\u20136.6 cm (centimeter-scale, profiled rows)\n- Displacement ranges: east (\u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m), north (0.029\u20130.058 m), up (0.051\u20130.224 m)\n- Sample spacing suggests ~1-second local cadence\n- qChannel values (1.3\u20132.4 million range) are opaque without decoding\n\n**Critical Profiling Limitations:**\n- Profile is scan-limited: only 5,000 of 250,000 rows profiled for numeric statistics\n- Full-file cadence, duration, temporal coverage, and gap analysis NOT verified from profiler evidence\n- Missing-value status for the full file NOT assessed\n- Metadata timestamp range (2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12) provided by resource metadata, not verified by profiler\n- Uncertainty values are descriptive statistics; no explicit noise or fitness criteria provided\n\n**Suitability Assessment:**\nMTA1 offers optimal geographic positioning for downtown LA seismic deformation monitoring with centimeter-level measurement precision. The staged CSV contains required columns with no nulls in sampled rows and uncertainties appropriate for regional seismic analysis. However, full-file data quality (cadence, continuity, gaps) remains unverified due to profiling scope. The station is suitable as the primary analysis station for the region, with nearby PKRD, ELSC, and USC2 available for multi-station validation."}}}

