event: message.part.completed
id: 223
data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:49:59.255721+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_0d94515cedad", "message_id": "msg_asst_ccd8c7ddaab2", "part_id": "part_633b744090fd", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "**EVENT CATALOG CAPABILITY GAP**\n\nThis analysis pack does not include a live earthquake catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API, SCEDC real-time catalog, or equivalent). Therefore, seismic event context for the Los Angeles region during 2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12 cannot be retrieved or verified.\n\n**What is missing:**\nTo contextualize the MTA1 GNSS displacement data with earthquake/seismic event information, the workflow would require:\n- A live USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API tool or equivalent\n- Access to a regional earthquake catalog (e.g., Southern California Earthquake Data Center, Caltech/USGS SCEDC)\n- Ability to query events by magnitude, location (lat/lon/depth), and time window\n- Optional: Felt reports, ShakeMap intensity data, or damage assessments from USGS\n\n**Impact:**\nThe GNSS displacement time-series from MTA1 is staged and profiled, but seismic event context (What earthquakes occurred? When? Where? Magnitude?) cannot be added without a working catalog tool. The analysis can proceed with displacement-only interpretation, but earthquake event attribution remains unavailable.\n\n**Next action:** To complete the seismic activity exploration, integrate or call a live earthquake catalog tool after this workflow.\n\n"}}

