data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:49:59.283675+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_6cd8cf4b5da6481b", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_be7e4295c87a", "workspace_id": "ws_9f03590dd4d4", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_0d94515cedad", "turn_id": "msg_user_0d94515cedad", "span_id": "sem_6cd8cf4b5da6481b", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert analysis produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:49:59.273380+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "analysis"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "main"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "analysis", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'analysis'.", "answer": "**EarthScope GNSS Analysis Summary: MTA1 Station Context for Los Angeles Seismic Deformation**\n\n**Data Acquisition & Profile:**\nThe MTA1 station time-series (MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv, 50.4 MB, 250,000 rows) contains all required GNSS displacement columns: time, east, north, up displacements, and corresponding uncertainties (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU). The profiled sample (5,000 rows) shows centimeter-scale measurement uncertainties and zero null values, with displacement ranges from \u22120.07 to +0.22 m across components. The profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence, duration, and gap quality were not verified.\n\n**Station Suitability:**\nMTA1 is geographically optimal for Los Angeles seismic deformation monitoring, positioned at the city center (0.3 km from region center, 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W). The station is the closest candidate within a dense 155-station EarthScope network spanning 100 km radius. Displacement uncertainties (3.2\u20133.6 cm horizontal, 6.2\u20136.6 cm vertical) are centimeter-scale, appropriate for regional deformation analysis. Alternative nearby stations (PKRD at 2.2 km, ELSC at 4.1 km, USC2 at 5.0 km) are available for multi-station validation.\n\n**Event Context Limitation:**\nThis analysis pack lacks a live earthquake catalog tool (USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API or equivalent). Seismic event context (magnitudes, depths, epicenters, timing) for the 2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12 window cannot be retrieved. The GNSS displacement time-series is staged and analyzed, but earthquake event attribution remains unavailable without external catalog integration.\n\n**Analysis Scope & Caveats:**\n- Profile is scan-limited to 5,000 of 250,000 rows for numeric statistics\n- Full-file temporal cadence, duration, gap analysis, and completeness not verified\n- qChannel quality flag values are opaque without decoding\n- Metadata timestamp range (2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12) from resource metadata, not tool-verified\n- Suitability assessment is preliminary pending full-file verification", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "The analysis expert has received completed results from all three child experts:\n\n1. **gnss_timeseries_analysis** (\u2713 complete): Successfully profiled the staged MTA1 CSV, confirming all 8 required GNSS columns present with centimeter-scale uncertainties and scan-limited profile coverage (5,000 of 250,000 rows profiled).\n\n2. **station_network_analysis** (\u2713 complete): Assessed MTA1 as geographically optimal (0.3 km from LA center) within a dense 155-station network, with centimeter-precision displacement measurements and alternative nearby stations (PKRD, ELSC, USC2) available for cross-validation.\n\n3. **seismic_event_catalog** (\u2713 complete): Returned explicit capability gap\u2014no live USGS earthquake catalog tool available in this pack, preventing event-context retrieval. This is an honest blocker, not a data failure.\n\n**Analysis branch completion status:**\nAll required and optional child work is done. The analysis branch has produced:\n- \u2713 Grounded profile evidence (child-generated)\n- \u2713 Grounded network suitability assessment (child-generated)\n- \u2713 Explicit event-context limitation (child-generated)\n- \u2713 Merged typed workflow_state with all evidence forwarded verbatim\n\n**Routing decision:**\nThe analysis expert's work is complete. All children have returned. The workflow_state is ready to return to the parent orchestrator, which will determine whether to continue to visualization and synthesis based on the user's full original request."}}}

