er, regional station density (155 candidates within 100 km), and any suitability limitations.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n(To be populated by synthesis after station network analysis and event-context analysis complete.)\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": true, \"local_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"metadata_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 50424246, \"source_url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"status\": \"staged\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 100, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Search radius of 100 km assumed as default for regional GNSS and seismic analysis; not specified in request\"]}, \"pipeline\": [\"geospatial\", \"data\", \"analysis\", \"visualization\", \"synthesis\"], \"profile\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"scan_limited\": true, \"status\": \"complete\"}, \"request\": \"Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles with EarthScope GNSS context and artifact\", \"resource_candidate\": {\"geographically_grounded\": true, \"station_id\": \"MTA1\", \"status\": \"selected\"}, \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 155, \"status\": \"ranked\"}, \"status\": \"analysis_profiling_complete; routing_to_network_analysis\"}}", "output_summary": "**MTA1 Station Suitability Assessment for Los Angeles Seismic Deformation Analysis**\n\n**Station Selection Rationale:**\nMTA1 is geographically optimal for capturing Los Angeles-area seismic deformation, positioned at the city center (0.3 km from region center, 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W) within a dense 155-station EarthScope network spanning 100 km radius.\n\n**Resource Evidence:**\n- Staged CSV: MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv (50.4 MB, 250,000 rows)\n- Network: CI (California Integrated Seismic Network)\n- Required columns: all present \u2713\n- Data rows: 250,000 available for analysis\n\n**Measurement Characteristics (Profiled Sample):**\n- Horizontal displacement uncertainties: 3.2\u20133.6 cm (east/north components)\n- Vertical displacement uncertainty: 6.2\u20136.6 cm\n- Displacement ranges: east (\u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m), north (0.029\u20130.058 m), up (0.051\u20130.224 m)\n- Null values in profiled rows: zero across all columns\n- Sample temporal spacing: ~1-second local cadence (unverified for full file)\n\n**Network Context & Redundancy:**\n- Closest station by far within the ranked 155-candidate network\n- Alternative stations for cross-validation within 6 km: PKRD (2.2 km), ELSC (4.1 km), USC2 (5.0 km)\n- Excellent network density supports multi-station deformation analysis if required\n\n**Limitations & Caveats:**\n- Profile scope: scan-limited to 5,000 rows (profiled of 250,000 total)\n- Full-file cadence, duration, gap analysis, and data completeness NOT verified\n- Vertical uncertainties (~6.5 cm) are centimeter-scale, appropriate but not sub-centimeter\n- qChannel quality flag is opaque without decoding\n- Metadata timestamp range (2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12) from resource metadata, not tool-verified\n\n**Suitability Conclusion:**\nMTA1 provides geographically grounded, centimeter-precision displacement measurements suitable for preliminary seismic deformation analysis in Los Angeles. Full-file temporal continuity and processing latency remain unverified. The station is recommended as the primary analysis platform for this workflow.", "return_output_summary": "**MTA1 Station Suitability Assessment for Los Angeles Seismic Deformation Analysis**\n\n**Station Selection Rationale:**\nMTA1 is geographically optimal for capturing Los Angeles-area seismic deformation, positioned at the city center (0.3 km from region center, 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W) within a dense 155-station EarthScope network spanning 100 km radius.\n\n**Resource Evidence:**\n- Staged CSV: MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv (50.4 MB, 250,000 rows)\n- Network: CI (California Integrated Seismic Network)\n- Required columns: all present \u2713\n- Data rows: 250,000 available for analysis\n\n**Measurement Characteristics (Profiled Sample):**\n- Horizontal displacement uncertainties: 3.2\u20133.6 cm (east/north components)\n- Vertical displacement uncertainty: 6.2\u20136.6 cm\n- Displacement ranges: east (\u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m), north (0.029\u20130.058 m), up (0.051\u20130.224 m)\n- Null values in profiled rows: zero across all columns\n- Sample temporal spacing: ~1-second local cadence (unverified for full file)\n\n**Network Context & Redundancy:**\n- Closest station by far within the ranked 155-candidate network\n- Alternative stations for cross-validation within 6 km: PKRD (2.2 km), ELSC (4.1 km), USC2 (5.0 km)\n- Excellent network density supports multi-station deformation analysis if required\n\n**Limitations & Caveats:**\n- Profile scope: scan-limited to 5,000 rows (profiled of 250,000 total)\n- Full-file cadence, duration, gap analysis, and data completeness NOT verified\n- Vertical uncertainties (~6.5 cm) are centimeter-scale, appropriate but not sub-centimeter\n- qChannel quality flag is opaque without 