id: 276
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:52:01.458540+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_39cbcf3b338545d3", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_be7e4295c87a", "workspace_id": "ws_9f03590dd4d4", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_0d94515cedad", "turn_id": "msg_user_0d94515cedad", "span_id": "sem_39cbcf3b338545d3", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert synthesis produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-25T22:52:01.409335+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "synthesis"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "main"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "synthesis", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'synthesis'.", "answer": "## Region\n\nLos Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States. Geographic center resolved to 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W via OpenStreetMap Nominatim geocoding. Analysis conducted within a 100 km search radius (assumed default; not specified in request).\n\n## Station selected\n\nStation **MTA1** \u2014 the geographically optimal EarthScope GNSS candidate at 0.3 km from the region center. Closest of 155 ranked nearby stations within the 100 km radius. Selected as the primary station for displacement analysis.\n\n## Data resource\n\n- **Staged CSV**: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **Source URL**: `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **File size**: 50.4 MB (50,424,246 bytes)\n- **Total rows**: 250,000 GNSS time-series observations\n\n## Profile evidence\n\nAll required GNSS displacement columns present: time, east, north, up, plus uncertainty estimates (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU) and quality flags (qChannel).\n\n**Profiled sample** (5,000 of 250,000 rows): \n- Displacement ranges \u2014 East: \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m; North: 0.029 to 0.058 m; Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m\n- Displacement uncertainties \u2014 East/North: 3.2\u20133.6 cm; Up: 6.2\u20136.6 cm (centimeter-scale precision)\n- Null values: zero across all columns in profiled rows\n\n**Profiling limitations**: Scan-limited to 5,000 rows. Full-file temporal cadence, duration, gap analysis, and completeness not verified. Uncertainty ranges reflect profiled sample statistics only.\n\n## Visualization\n\n- **PNG artifact**: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1_timeseries_displacement.png`\n- **Content**: Multi-panel time-series showing east, north, and up displacement components on shared UTC time axis\n- **Data coverage**: 2000 rows plotted from the 250,000-row CSV\n- **Title**: \"MTA1 GNSS Displacement Time Series (East, North, Up) \u2014 Los Angeles Region\"\n\nThe artifact visualizes displacement patterns suitable for regional seismic deformation discussion.\n\n## Freshness, coverage & provenance limitations\n\n**Data freshness**: Temporal coverage 2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12 (recent, per resource metadata; full-file span not tool-verified).\n\n**Analysis scope**: Profile is scan-limited; only 5,000 rows examined for min/max/mean statistics, and only 2000 rows plotted. Full-file cadence, duration, gap quality, and missing-value prevalence across all 250,000 rows remain unverified.\n\n**Earthquake context**: This analysis pack does not include a live USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API or equivalent earthquake catalog tool. Seismic event context (magnitudes, depths, epicenters, felt reports) for the 2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12 window cannot be retrieved. Displacement data are available for analysis, but event attribution and correlation with specific earthquakes require external catalog integration.\n\n**Suitability**: MTA1 provides geographically grounded GNSS displacement measurements at centimeter-scale precision, appropriate for preliminary seismic deformation analysis. Station assessment is pending full-file temporal, quality, and gap verification.", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "The synthesis expert has received complete grounded evidence from all upstream experts:\n\n1. **Geospatial**: Los Angeles resolved to precise coordinates (34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W) with 100 km search radius via OSM Nominatim geocoding, high confidence.\n\n2. **Data**: EarthScope GNSS discovery completed \u2014 155 nearby stations identified within the radius; MTA1 selected as the closest candidate (0.3 km from center). Real time-series CSV staged at the absolute path from `acquisition.local_path` (250,000 rows, 50.4 MB).\n\n3. **Analysis**: MTA1 profile completed. All required GNSS displacement columns present (time, east, north, up). Profiled 5,000 of 250,000 rows for numeric statistics. Centimeter-scale displacement uncertainties confirmed (3.2\u20133.6 cm horizontal, 6.2\u20136.6 cm vertical). Full-file cadence, duration, and gap quality not verified (scan-limited profile).\n\n4. **Visualization**: PNG time-series artifact successfully created at exact path from `artifact.path`. Shows all three displacement components (east, north, up) over 2000 plotted rows on shared UTC time axis.\n\n5. **Event context**: Blocked by missing live earthquake catalog tool \u2014 honest limitation, not a staging failure. GNSS displacement data available, but seismic event attribution (magnitudes, depths, epicenters) unavailable.\n\n**Synthesis task**: Merge all evidence into a final brief suitable for discussing seismic deformation patterns, with full disclosure of limitations."}}}

