tus": "complete"}, "request": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles with EarthScope GNSS context and artifact", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "status": "analysis_complete_event_catalog_blocked"}, "tools_called": [], "children": []}, {"agent_id": "analysis", "parent_id": "main", "dispatch_target": "analysis", "status": "completed", "stage": "parent.resumed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "resumed_from": "seismic_event_catalog", "return_payload": "compact_result", "depth": 0, "output_summary": "**EVENT CATALOG CAPABILITY GAP**\n\nThis analysis pack does not include a live earthquake catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API, SCEDC real-time catalog, or equivalent). Therefore, seismic event context for the Los Angeles region during 2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12 cannot be retrieved or verified.\n\n**What is missing:**\nTo contextualize the MTA1 GNSS displacement data with earthquake/seismic event information, the workflow would require:\n- A live USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API tool or equivalent\n- Access to a regional earthquake catalog (e.g., Southern California Earthquake Data Center, Caltech/USGS SCEDC)\n- Ability to query events by magnitude, location (lat/lon/depth), and time window\n- Optional: Felt reports, ShakeMap intensity data, or damage assessments from USGS\n\n**Impact:**\nThe GNSS displacement time-series from MTA1 is staged and profiled, but seismic event context (What earthquakes occurred? When? Where? Magnitude?) cannot be added without a working catalog tool. The analysis can proceed with displacement-only interpretation, but earthquake event attribution remains unavailable.\n\n**Next action:** To complete the seismic activity exploration, integrate or call a live earthquake catalog tool after this workflow.", "return_output_summary": "**EVENT CATALOG CAPABILITY GAP**\n\nThis analysis pack does not include a live earthquake catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API, SCEDC real-time catalog, or equivalent). Therefore, seismic event context for the Los Angeles region during 2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12 cannot be retrieved or verified.\n\n**What is missing:**\nTo contextualize the MTA1 GNSS displacement data with earthquake/seismic event information, the workflow would require:\n- A live USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API tool or equivalent\n- Access to a regional earthquake catalog (e.g., Southern California Earthquake Data Center, Caltech/USGS SCEDC)\n- Ability to query events by magnitude, location (lat/lon/depth), and time window\n- Optional: Felt reports, ShakeMap intensity data, or damage assessments from USGS\n\n**Impact:**\nThe GNSS displacement time-series from MTA1 is staged and profiled, but seismic event context (What earthquakes occurred? When? Where? Magnitude?) cannot be added without a working catalog tool. The analysis can proceed with displacement-only interpretation, but earthquake event attribution remains unavailable.\n\n**Next action:** To complete the seismic activity exploration, integrate or call a live earthquake catalog tool after this workflow.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Search radius of 100 km assumed as default for regional GNSS and seismic analysis; not specified in request"]}, "network_analysis": {"distance_from_center_km": 0.3, "limitations": ["scan_limited_profile", "full_file_cadence_not_verified", "full_file_duration_not_verified", "gap_analysis_not_performed", "missing_values_full_file_not_assessed"], "measurement_scale": "centimeter", "nearby_alternatives": ["PKRD", "ELSC", "USC2"], "network_candidates": 155, "primary_station": "MTA1", "status": "complete", "suitability": "geographically_grounded_preliminary"}, "pipeline": ["geospatial", "data", "analysis", "visualization", "synthesis"], "profile": {"path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "scan_limited": true, "status": "complete"}, "request": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles with EarthScope GNSS context and artifact", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "status": "analysis_complete_event_catalog_blocked", "event_context": {"blocker": "no live event catalog tool available in this pack", "limitations": ["no_live_event_catalog_tool"], "next_action": "add or call a live earthquake/event catalog tool for event counts, magnitudes, and dates", "status": "blocked", "verified_event_count": null}}}]}, {"agent_id": "main", "parent_id": "", "dispatch_target": "main", "status": "completed", "stage": "parent.resumed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "resumed_from": "analysis", "return_payload": "compact_result", "depth": 0, "output_summary": "**EarthScope GNSS Analysis Summary: MTA1 Station Context for Los Angeles Seismic Deformation**\n\n**Data Acquisition & Profile:**\nThe MTA1 station time-series (MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv, 50.4 MB, 250,000 rows) contains all required GNSS displacement columns: time, east, north, up displacements, and corresponding uncertainties (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU). The profiled sample (5,000 rows) shows centimeter-scale measurement uncertainties and zero null values, with displacement ranges from \u22120.07 to +0.22 m across components. The profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence, duration, and gap quality were not verified.\n\n**Station Suitability:**\nMTA1 is geographically optimal for Los Angeles seismic deformation monitoring, positioned at the city center (0.3 km from region center, 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W). The station is the closest candidate within a dense 155-station EarthScope network spanning 100 km radius. Displacement uncertainties (3.2\u20133.6 cm horizontal, 6.2\u20136.6 cm vertical) are centimeter-scale, appropriate for regional deformation analysis. Alternative nearby stations (PKRD at 2.2 km, ELSC at 4.1 km, USC2 at 5.0 km) are available for multi-station validation.\n\n**Event Context Limitation:**\nThis analysis pack lacks a live earthquake catalog tool (USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API or equivalent). Seismic event context (magnitudes, depths, epicenters, timing) for the 2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12 window cannot be retrieved. The GNSS displacement time-series is staged and analyzed, but earthquake event attribution remains unavailable without external catalog integration.\n\n**Analysis Scope & Caveats:**\n- Profile is scan-limited to 5,000 of 250,000 rows for numeric statistics\n- Full-file temporal cadence, duration, gap analysis, and completeness not verified\n- qChannel quality flag values are opaque without decoding\n- Metadata timestamp range (2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12) from resource metadata, not tool-verified\n- Suitability assessment is preliminary pending full-file verification", "return_output_summary": "**EarthScope GNSS Analysis Summary: MTA1 Station Context for Los Angeles Seismic Deformation**\n\n**Data Acquisition & Profile:**\nThe MTA1 station time-series (MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv, 50.4 MB, 250,000 rows) contains all required GNSS displacement columns: time, east, north, up displacements, and corresponding uncertainties (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU). The profiled sample (5,000 rows) shows centimeter-scale measurement uncertainties and zero null values, with displacement ranges from \u22120.07 to +0.22 m across components. The profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence, duration, and gap quality were not verified.\n\n**Station Suitability:**\nMTA1 is geographically optimal for Los Angeles seismic deformation monitoring, positioned at the city center (0.3 km from region center, 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W). The station is the closest candidate within a dense 155-station EarthScope network spanning 100 km radius. Displacement uncertainties (3.2\u20133.6 cm horizontal, 6.2\u20136.6 cm vertical) are centimeter-scale, appropriate for regional deformation analysis. Alternative nearby stations (PKRD at 2.2 km, ELSC at 4.1 km, USC2 at 5.0 km) are available for multi-station validation.\n\n**Event Context Limitation:**\nThis analysis pack lacks a live earthquake catalog tool (USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API or equivalent). Seismic event context (magnitudes, depths, epicenters, timing) for the 2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12 window cannot be retrieved. The GNSS displacement time-series is staged and analyzed, but earthquake event attribution remains unavailable without external catalog integration.\n\n**Analysis Scope & Caveats:**\n- Profile is scan-limited to 5,000 of 250,000 rows for numeric statistics\n- Full-file temporal cadence, duration, gap analysis, and completeness not verified\n- qChannel quality flag values are opaque without decoding\n- Metadata timestamp range (2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12) from resource metadata, not tool-verified\n- Suitability assessment is preliminary pending full-file 